The sentinel validator proposed for budlum (SENTINEL, RoleId 10) carries
BudFly's frozen 48-tick anchors as audit evidence. Lubot's side of that
contract is a pure byte table it can check claims against with zero
simulation and zero I/O:

- GOLDEN_PINS: the four externally frozen sentinel cases, bytes copied
  verbatim from crates/budfly/goldens.anchor.toml (BudFly PR #5)
- BUDFLY_MANIFEST_ROOT_SHA256: sha256 of that manifest at pinning time;
  a reviewer re-hashes the upstream file instead of trusting this copy
- RING_BUMP_ANCHOR: the pinned compass-attractor bump (64 ticks)
- pinned_anchor / evidence_matches / ring_bump_matches: fail-closed
  only (unknown digest -> None; one flipped bit -> false)
- digest binding documented: bytes 10..16 and 20..32 carry no signal in
  the frozen stimulus, and the crate says so next to the table

CRATES.md gains its fourteenth row.
